Changelog: 16-11-2026 00:48:58

Fixed. Every action in the helpers is the suite's pill (core's ActionPill), as in the other apps, instead of a small
button: the list's helpers, Refresh, Install all and each group's Install, Turn on and Turn off, MangoHud Config's
actions. MangoHud Config has its FPS log actions on a row of their own, so no pill is squeezed.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 23:41:16

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 19:43:21

Added. Two helpers for the kernel's arguments: IOMMU Off (amd_iommu=off, Board Test's test 23) and CPU Mitigations
Off (mitigations=off, test 24). Turn on adds the argument with rpm-ostree kargs after the password (pkexec) and
notes in /var/lib/bc250-helpers that the helper added it; Turn off removes only an argument the helper added. The
window shows the argument on the running kernel's command line and on the next boot's, who added it and, for the
IOMMU, its groups; after a change it says to restart the board (systemctl reboot) and never does. IOMMU Off is not
offered when the BIOS has the IOMMU off already.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 14:33:23

Added. BC-250 Helpers, small windows for one job each that come with the suite: Test Extras (the optional tools
Board Test's tests use, which are there and which tests use them, installed per group with Board Test's own
install-requirements.sh), MangoHud Config (opens or makes ~/.config/MangoHud/MangoHud.conf to edit and save, sets
the FPS log Board Test reads and makes its folder, deletes logs older than 30 days), Fix GPU Metrics (fix-metrics
and the method in the GPU governor's config.toml, after a dated backup, and a restart of a running governor),
Sensors Module (forces the nct6683 driver for the board's SuperIO chip at boot, offered only when neither nct6683
nor nct6687 serves it), Game Memory Map (vm.max_map_count in /etc/sysctl.d) and Persistent Journal
(/var/log/journal). The four that change the board ask for the password with pkexec, turn on only what is off and
turn off only what they turned on. bc250-helpers opens the list of helpers, bc250-helpers <key> one helper.
